[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Not Guilty]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.44]Lesson 11 | 第11课
[00:02.11]Not guilty | 无罪
[00:08.86]What was the Customs Officer looking for? | 海关官员在找什么？
[00:13.22]Customs Officers are quite tolerant these days, but they can still stop you when you are going through the Green Channel and have nothing to declare. | 如今的海关官员往往相当宽容，但即便你走绿色通道、没有任何东西要申报，他们仍可以拦住你。
[00:23.00]Even really honest people are often made to feel guilty. | 甚至连完全诚实的人也常被弄得觉得自己有罪似的。
[00:27.47]The hardened professional smuggler, on the other hand, is never troubled by such feelings, | 而老练的职业走私犯却从不为这种感觉所困扰，
[00:33.67]even if he has five hundred gold watches hidden in his suitcase. | 哪怕他的手提箱里藏着500块金表。
[00:38.97]When I returned from abroad recently, a particularly officious young Customs Officer | 最近一次回国时，一位特别爱管闲事的年轻海关官员
[00:44.92]clearly regarded me as a smuggler. | 显然把我当成了走私犯。
[00:48.39]'Have you anything to declare?' he asked, looking me in the eye. | “有什么要申报的吗？”他直盯着我的眼睛问。
[00:54.07]'No,' I answered confidently. | “没有。”我自信地回答。
[00:57.61]'Would you mind unlocking this suitcase please? ' | “请打开这只手提箱好吗？”
[01:01.55]'Not at all,' I answered. | “没问题。”我回答说。
[01:03.97]The Officer went through the case with great care. | 那位官员极为仔细地翻看了这只箱子。
[01:07.71]All the things I had packed so carefully were soon in a dreadful mess. | 我收拾得整整齐齐的东西一下子被翻得乱七八糟。
[01:13.57]I felt sure I would never be able to close the case again. | 我感到这只箱子恐怕再也合不上了。
[01:18.27]Suddenly, I saw the Officer's face light up. | 突然，我看见官员的脸上露出了得意的神色。
[01:22.34]He had spotted a tiny bottle at the bottom of my case | 他在我的箱底发现了一只小瓶子，
[01:26.25]and he pounced on it with delight. | 便欣喜地把它抓在手中。
[01:29.35]'Perfume, eh?' he asked sarcastically. | “香水，嗯？”他讥讽地问道。
[01:34.68]'You should have declared that. | “你早该申报了。
[01:36.66]Perfume is not exempt from import duty.  ' | 香水是不免进口税的。”
[01:41.38]'But it isn't perfume, I said. 'It's hair gel.  ' | “可这不是香水，”我说，“这是发胶。”
[01:46.96]Then I added with a smile, | 接着我笑着补充说：
[01:49.55]'It's a strange mixture I make myself. | “这是我自己配的一种奇怪的混合物。
[01:53.36]As I expected, he did not believe me. | 果然不出所料，他不相信我的话。
[01:57.25]'Try it!' I said encouragingly. | “试试吧！”我怂恿说。
[02:00.96]The Officer unscrewed the cap and put the bottle to his nostrils. | 那位官员拧开瓶盖，把瓶子凑到鼻子底下。
[02:05.46]He was greeted by an unpleasant smell which convinced him that I was telling the truth. | 一股难闻的气味扑面而来，这使他相信我说的是实话。
[02:11.96]A few minutes later, I was able to hurry away with precious chalk marks on my baggage. | 几分钟后，我终于得以匆匆离去，行李上带着珍贵的粉笔记号。
